+---
+title: "roottest io/json failures die in the translated constructor, not in jsonbuffer"
+kind: "gotcha"
+summary: "When an io/json test fails with TypeError 'NoneType' object is not subscriptable, look at the emitted constructor for a multi-dim char[N][M] member before reading jsonbuffer."
+tags: [json, tbufferjson, pycxx, translator, roottest, char-array]
+created: "2026-11-21T06:21:31.358Z"
+updated: "2026-11-21T06:21:31.358Z"
+---
+`roottest/root/io/json` reports `TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not subscriptable` for `BasicTypes`, `Objects`, `STL` and `STL1`, but the failure is in translated C++, not in `pyroot/core/jsonbuffer.py`. Every one of them constructs `TJsonEx2` (from `roottest/root/io/json/test_classes.h`), which declares `char fChar[2][3][4]`; `src/xrdroot/pycxx/emit_vars.py`'s `_char_array` emits `self.fChar = array('char*', 2, [])` for a char array of more than one dimension, and the next statement, `self.fChar[i][j] = with_char(self.fChar[i][j], k, 0, True)`, then subscripts a `None` cell. The `run.log`'s position (`runBasicTypes.C:8`) is the declaration of `TJsonEx2`, so read the whole traceback, not just the last frame.
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    A["test_classes.h: char fChar[2][3][4]"] --> B["pycxx/emit_vars.py:_char_array"]
+    B --> C["self.fChar = array('char*', 2, [])"]
+    C --> D["two None cells"]
+    D --> E["self.fChar[i][j] = with_char(...)"]
+    E --> F["TypeError: NoneType is not subscriptable"]
+    F --> G["run.log says runBasicTypes.C:8"]
+    G --> H["jsonbuffer is never reached"]
+```
+
+## How to see it without the harness
+
+Run the macro directly in the harness's working copy, which has the `libJsonTestClasses` dictionary built:
+
+```
+cd /tmp/r30/run-w04/work/roottest/root/io/json
+export PYTHONPATH=$PWD/src
+$PY -c "from xrdroot.pycint.execute import run_and_quit; run_and_quit('runBasicTypes.C')"
+```
+
+That prints the Python traceback into the generated library (`<translation of .../libJsonTestClasses>`, `line 105, in __init__`), which the `xrdroot run` CLI hides behind one `MacroError` line. The emitted source is the `python` key of the `.xrdlib` JSON next to it (`jq -r .python libJsonTestClasses.xrdlib`).
+
+## The repair, and what it should turn green
+
+A `char[N][M]` is N rows of C strings, each `M-1` characters and a NUL — the object's own nesting is what `jsonbuffer`'s `_char_rows`/`_char_strings` walk — so `_char_array` must emit nested rows of `''` rather than one `array('char*', N, [])`. Patching only that generated line in a scratch work dir (`self.fChar = [['', '', ''], ['', '', '']]`) makes `runBasicTypes` and `runObjects` exit 0 with stdout byte-identical to `BasicTypes.ref` and `Objects.ref` under `tools/rootsuite/refdiff.custom_diff`; no jsonbuffer change is needed for either. `STL`/`STL1` need more even then: `jsonbuffer._restore` still refuses a container member holding values, and `TJsonEx12` holds `std::vector<TJsonEx9>`, whose `TString** fStr6[3]` is the same refusal that leaves `StreamerLoop` UNSUPPORTED.
